{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J4 0a94 LANDED-FOR-REVIEW. Full suite 7553 passed / 29 skipped / 114 deselected / 0 FAILED in 30m54s (up from 7533 at J2 — J4's new tests).\nSTAGING CARE: J3's happy-path test file was already in the working tree and still RED at this point, so I staged J4's four files EXPLICITLY rather than 'git add -A'. Verified the staged set before committing; the red J3 file stayed unstaged. A blanket add would have committed a failing test and drawn a Verified -1.\nAlso confirmed the full-suite run was not polluted by those J3 files: pytest collects at startup and they were created after the run began, which is consistent with 0 failures and why I waited for this suite to finish before letting any implementer touch the tree again.\nCommit 3c6220235, 4 files, +567/-30. Trailers: rebar-ticket 0a94 + Change-Id + Signed-off-by. 50/72 hook passed.\nGERRIT CHANGE 1011 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1011 — stacked on 1010 (J2). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\nSTACK SO FAR: 1009 (J1, MERGED) <- 1010 (J2, both gates green) <- 1011 (J4, pending). J3 commits next on top."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785351469263715001,"uuid":"014d9aba-b930-4746-8835-574949dea04e"}